n't the  perfect gift for your ten-year-old the  devs have said that the world is noir  themed  just like Blade Runner where it's a  pretty depressing place to live  this is juxtaposed against the roaring  sunshine and bright neon lights  cyberpunk 2077 will almost certainly be  given an 18 or adult rating if that one  mission is the benchmark Knight city  will be our new home which sits in  between San Francisco and Santa Barbara  in the game this land was purchased by  Richard night in the hopes of creating a  safe city free of crime and oppression  as you can tell it didn't go according  to plan here in night city surviving the  day is an achievement in itself the  world is cutthroat and deadly when  Richard Knight built the city he left  out criminal corporations after four  years they became a little annoyed and  killed him taking over the projects  before eventually being pushed down by  the mega corporations we will fill the  boots of V a cyber enhance Street  warrior who you build from scratch will  your V be male or female maybe a few  tattoos to look edgy or what about a new  haircut complete with LED lighting CD  Projekt RED wants this character to  represent you so unlike The Witcher  where we're stuck with Geralt in  cyberpunk 2077 we have full agency over  our character even the backstory is  customizable to give your character  the upbringing they deserved and just in  case you're wondering all voice lines  have been recorded in both a masculine  gruff voice and the more delicate  feminine manner your character will have  many stats to improve and upgrade  including the typical RPG traditions  strength intelligence Constitution  reflexes and is another one called cool  I received conflicting reports on how  cool operates in the game some people  state it's about your characters ability  to keep calm under pressure whereas  other outlets suggests that cool works  in conjunction with the street cred  mechanic when hopping around the city  the higher the street credibility the  more options unlock whether that's the  prices at your local black market or  dialogue options which were previously  hidden from view oh and the freakin  awesome LED neon jacket v's wearing here  this will give you an instant boost to  your street cred come on that's a darn  cool jacket and you just know there is  going to be a collector's edition with  that jacket a general class system will  be at work in cyberpunk 2077 thanks to  cyber wear which allows for biotech  upgrades of V think of it like Deus Ex  and the neuro mods and enhancements the  three classes we can obtain are  netrunner for hacking abilities techie  which allows for renegade off-market  tech to be used and developed and  finally the solo class which is  essentially a trained killer like a  soldier or assassin the glasses are not  cut and dry though they can be combined  so if you'd like to use the Mantis  blades as seen in the original trailer  they'll be here but maybe you'll also  upgrade your netrunner abilities and  tack a few enemy augments at first  glance the freedom to play your way is  phenomenal probably the biggest  information to take from the initial  reveal of cyberpunk 2077 is the  viewpoint will be playing in  first-person perspective the devs have  made a very strict statement and are  pushing that it's not a first-person  shooter with RPG elements it's a  role-playing game first and foremost set  in first-person with some shooting  elements does that mean the gunplay is  as solid as Borderlands or destiny or  will it be a little more clunky like  fallout 4 from the one level we've seen  you've got nothing to worry about the  gunplay is solid as a rock  going back to classes for a moment did  you ever play cyberpunk 2013 of 2020  they were tabletop RPGs you know the  kind where you have so many dice it's  like a Christie  No well in cyberpunk 2020 there were 10  character roles we've already talked  about three of them solo techy netrunner  the others although not playable will  make up the lore elements around  cyberpunk 2077 within gangs and  communities the rocker boys use music  and the desire to oppose the corporate  juggernauts as a shared mentality the  nomads are road warriors that loosely  resemble a gypsy community the fixers  dealing information and knowledge add to  this the police force the corporate  regimes and the media outlets that deal  in propaganda and we've got a deep  gaming world to investigate so what  about combat inside the punk  although the RPG elements take center  stage the game is filled with  opportunities to go on the rampage the  standard cover shooting is here if  that's your bag but why not upgrade your  augments to allow for matrix style  slow-motion effects are kung fu movie  knee slides and double jumps these moves  are best suited to a solo build but if  you prefer the netrunner abilities then  you'll be able to hack into the enemy if  you can find a way to get close enough  to jack in the net runner has so many  unique skills to play with and the demo  show definitely focused on that  character build some of the coolest  things talks about behind closed doors  were about the tech on offer in the open  world there's a scanner that allows you  to see behind enemy cover there's a  weapon which will shoot straight through  that cover there's even a weapon type  which allows for bullets to deliberately  bounce from wall to wall and ricochet  into unsuspecting enemies there's even a  high level rifle called the smart rifle  which will track enemy movement and we  haven't even spoke about melee options  putting all these action elements  together and we've got one hell of a  video game let's jump back into law in  the game world again remember five and a  half years ago when the first teaser  trailer dropped it looked as if the  police force were attempting to take  down an unhinged citizen this  mantis-like lady has cyber psychosis  which is such a widespread issue that  there is a dedicated police task force  focused on bringing cyber psychos down  in the world of cyberpunk 2020 the more  augments a human added to their body the  more their brain would detach from  humanity then suddenly they would snap  completely with an uncontrollable desire  to kill every man and woman  they set their eyes upon this really  puts into perspective the harsh nature  of night cities  due to the size of the world travel  options will be imperative the Metro  subway is a great way to quickly get to  generally the right area but there are  cars and motorbikes to ride upon to  violence will follow you around the city  and this is where the camera can break  from first-person when driving a  third-person camera is possible and in  the footage we saw v asked an NPC to  drive while she shot the crap out of the  cars following them another vehicle  we've seen in the trailer are these  ships or hovercrafts but a last CD  Projekt RED don't want to talk about  these just yet so how does the world  tied together in cyberpunk 2077 in  addition to the typical quest lines you  are able to acquire quest from countless  NPCs just like in The Witcher 3 your  skills as a mercenary unlock further  quests to divert from the core story  it's even possible to stumble across  Equestria by overhearing Intel or  joining a random gunfight across the  street it's all about organic  storytelling there's even talk of a  multiplayer component which could be  added post launch more info on that as  we find out but at the moment it's only  a concept so let's move on did you spot  any easter eggs in the cyberpunk reveal  trailer I absolutely adore Easter eggs  and video games there's a handful here  so let's quickly look at them during the  shot of the metro map at the start of  the trailer take note of the n6m a wood  or eight one six reference number this  is a nod to Blade Runner and Roy batty  serial number he was the leader of the  renegade Nexus 6 group played  brilliantly if I grow to get our there's  some graffiti on the wall outside the  motel which reads he is Johnny arguably  a nod to the shiny and this scene  here's Johnny but most likely this is a  reference to a character in cyberpunk  2020 who was a famous rocker boy singer  and guitarist during the reveal on the  Xbox stage mindless text filled the  screen as if the stage was been hacked  but these jumbled numbers and letters  were actually gain codes  allowing those who paid attention the  opportunity to download The Witcher and  the DLCs - oh there's another one at the  end of the trailer for a split second  was another text field image to read  this is a personally written message to  the cyberpunk community thanking them  for their patience promising no DRM on  the PC and most noticeably laughing at  the thought of microtransactions you've  just got a love CD Projekt RED to end  let's talk about a release date at  present there is no plans to reveal a  release here nevermind a month so let's  start a competition when do you think  cyberpunk 2077 will be releasing throw  down your year and month guesses the  winner will be pinned in all its glory  my guess is September 2020 so they have  it cyberpunk 2077 looks like The Witcher  and Deus Ex smash together for me  that sounds bility awesome what do you  reckon is it worth the hype I'd love to  know your thoughts I'm Adam from  Playstation grenade as always it's been  a pleasure  I'll see you next  [Music]

